1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,084
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:04,084 --> 00:00:08,534
Everyday conversations for adults!

3
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Greetings and Gym Conversation

4
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:14,461
Good morning!

5
00:00:14,485 --> 00:00:17,876
Oh, good morning!

6
00:00:17,899 --> 00:00:21,267
Lovely weather today, isn't it?

7
00:00:21,291 --> 00:00:25,557
Yes, it's really nice out.

8
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:29,514
But it's a little hot, though.

9
00:00:29,537 --> 00:00:31,886
Yeah, it is.

10
00:00:31,909 --> 00:00:35,708
It's been hot every day lately.

11
00:00:35,731 --> 00:00:40,431
Do you come to this gym often, Suzuki?

12
00:00:40,454 --> 00:00:43,758
Yeah, I do.

13
00:00:43,782 --> 00:00:47,891
How many times a week do you come?

14
00:00:47,914 --> 00:00:51,989
About three times a week.

15
00:00:52,013 --> 00:00:56,807
Three times a week? That's impressive!

16
00:00:56,830 --> 00:01:00,330
How about you, Emma? Do you come often?

17
00:01:00,353 --> 00:01:04,900
Just once a week for me.

18
00:01:04,924 --> 00:01:07,057
I see.

19
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:10,952
What day do you usually come?

20
00:01:10,976 --> 00:01:14,321
Mostly Saturdays.

21
00:01:14,344 --> 00:01:19,921
I come on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Saturdays.

22
00:01:19,944 --> 00:01:23,977
So, I'll see you again on Saturday!

23
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,956
Yeah, sounds good!

24
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:31,846
By the way, what do you usually do at the gym?

25
00:01:31,869 --> 00:01:35,403
I usually go for a run.

26
00:01:35,425 --> 00:01:39,018
How long do you run for?

27
00:01:39,042 --> 00:01:42,942
About 30 minutes.

28
00:01:42,965 --> 00:01:47,235
30 minutes? Doesn't that tire you out?

29
00:01:47,259 --> 00:01:52,026
It does a little, but it feels great!

30
00:01:52,049 --> 00:01:55,616
I always swim.

31
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:58,506
You swim in the pool?

32
00:01:58,529 --> 00:02:02,666
Yeah, for about an hour.

33
00:02:02,689 --> 00:02:06,164
An hour? That's a long time!

34
00:02:06,188 --> 00:02:10,574
Yeah, I do get a little tired after that.

35
00:02:10,597 --> 00:02:14,394
What do you do after working out?

36
00:02:14,417 --> 00:02:18,766
I always drink some cold water.

37
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:23,027
I take a shower right away.

38
00:02:23,051 --> 00:02:25,984
And then what?

39
00:02:26,007 --> 00:02:30,604
I go grocery shopping and head home.

40
00:02:30,628 --> 00:02:33,728
For dinner?

41
00:02:33,751 --> 00:02:38,517
Yeah, I cook dinner myself.

42
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:41,315
That's great!

43
00:02:41,339 --> 00:02:45,906
Well, I'm off to take a shower.

44
00:02:45,929 --> 00:02:48,327
Good work today!

45
00:02:48,350 --> 00:02:51,892
Thanks, you too!

46
00:02:51,915 --> 00:02:54,584
See you Saturday!

47
00:02:54,608 --> 00:02:56,108
Scene 2: Lunchtime Conversation

48
00:02:56,108 --> 00:02:58,141
Hello!

49
00:02:58,164 --> 00:03:01,000
Oh, hi there!

50
00:03:01,024 --> 00:03:04,490
Are you about to have lunch?

51
00:03:04,513 --> 00:03:07,389
Yes, that's right.

52
00:03:07,413 --> 00:03:10,565
Where do you usually eat?

53
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:14,737
I always eat here in the break room.

54
00:03:14,761 --> 00:03:18,147
What's for lunch today?

55
00:03:18,170 --> 00:03:21,945
Just bread and coffee today.

56
00:03:21,968 --> 00:03:24,268
Bread, huh?

57
00:03:24,291 --> 00:03:28,425
Yeah, I bought it at the bakery in front of the station.

58
00:03:28,448 --> 00:03:32,814
Oh, that bakery is really good, isn’t it?

59
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:36,383
Yeah, it’s delicious.

60
00:03:36,407 --> 00:03:40,507
Emma, what are you having today?

61
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:44,038
I’ve got my homemade bento.

62
00:03:44,061 --> 00:03:46,694
Did you make it yourself?

63
00:03:46,717 --> 00:03:50,291
Yes, I make it every morning.

64
00:03:50,315 --> 00:03:52,748
That’s amazing!

65
00:03:52,771 --> 00:03:56,206
What did you make today?

66
00:03:56,229 --> 00:04:00,816
I made tamagoyaki and a meat dish.

67
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,907
Wow, that looks so good!

68
00:04:03,930 --> 00:04:06,230
Thank you!

69
00:04:06,253 --> 00:04:09,359
I just love cooking.

70
00:04:09,382 --> 00:04:13,491
Actually, I love cooking too.

71
00:04:13,515 --> 00:04:16,015
Really?

72
00:04:16,038 --> 00:04:18,871
Do you cook often?

73
00:04:18,894 --> 00:04:23,594
Yeah, I usually make dinner myself.

74
00:04:23,617 --> 00:04:26,884
What kind of dishes do you make?

75
00:04:26,907 --> 00:04:31,207
I often make curry or udon.

76
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:33,330
That’s great!

77
00:04:33,353 --> 00:04:36,923
Do you like Japanese food?

78
00:04:36,946 --> 00:04:40,127
Yes, I love it!

79
00:04:40,151 --> 00:04:43,227
What’s your favorite?

80
00:04:43,251 --> 00:04:47,386
Ramen is my favorite.

81
00:04:47,410 --> 00:04:50,768
Ramen is so good, right?

82
00:04:50,792 --> 00:04:55,471
Yeah. What about you, Emma?

83
00:04:55,494 --> 00:04:58,879
I love sushi.

84
00:04:58,903 --> 00:05:01,936
Do you go often?

85
00:05:01,959 --> 00:05:06,692
Yeah, I go with friends sometimes on weekends.

86
00:05:06,715 --> 00:05:09,382
Where do you go?

87
00:05:09,405 --> 00:05:13,401
We usually go to a sushi place in Shinjuku.

88
00:05:13,425 --> 00:05:15,458
That’s great!

89
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:19,078
I’m craving sushi now!

90
00:05:19,102 --> 00:05:23,004
Well then, how about we go together next time?

91
00:05:23,027 --> 00:05:27,399
Yes, I’d love to! I’m looking forward to it.

92
00:05:27,422 --> 00:05:28,922
Scene 3: Talking About Exercise

93
00:05:28,922 --> 00:05:31,655
Good work today.

94
00:05:31,678 --> 00:05:34,212
Good work today.

95
00:05:34,235 --> 00:05:37,868
Did you get a lot of exercise today?

96
00:05:37,891 --> 00:05:42,724
Yeah, I went for a run for about an hour.

97
00:05:42,747 --> 00:05:45,981
A whole hour?

98
00:05:46,004 --> 00:05:48,637
That’s amazing!

99
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:52,493
What about you, Emma?

100
00:05:52,516 --> 00:05:56,587
I swam a little at the pool.

101
00:05:56,611 --> 00:06:00,004
How long did you swim?

102
00:06:00,027 --> 00:06:03,294
About 40 minutes.

103
00:06:03,317 --> 00:06:06,217
Weren’t you tired?

104
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:12,229
No, I swam slowly, so I'm not too tired.

105
00:06:12,252 --> 00:06:17,786
Emma, you really love sports, don't you?

106
00:06:17,808 --> 00:06:20,975
Yes, I love it!

107
00:06:20,998 --> 00:06:24,505
What other sports do you like?

108
00:06:24,529 --> 00:06:28,429
I like tennis.

109
00:06:28,452 --> 00:06:32,157
Tennis? That sounds great!

110
00:06:32,181 --> 00:06:36,648
Suzuki, what sports do you like?

111
00:06:36,671 --> 00:06:40,664
I like soccer.

112
00:06:40,688 --> 00:06:43,921
Do you play soccer often?

113
00:06:43,944 --> 00:06:48,177
Yeah, I play with friends on weekends.

114
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:51,300
Where do you play?

115
00:06:51,323 --> 00:06:55,156
We play at a big park nearby.

116
00:06:55,179 --> 00:06:58,454
Is it fun?

117
00:06:58,477 --> 00:07:03,070
Yes, it's a lot of fun!

118
00:07:03,094 --> 00:07:06,161
Do you also like watching soccer?

119
00:07:06,184 --> 00:07:10,617
Yes, I often watch it on TV.

120
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:14,810
Which do you prefer, baseball or soccer?

121
00:07:14,833 --> 00:07:19,067
I like soccer better.

122
00:07:19,090 --> 00:07:21,794
I see.

123
00:07:21,818 --> 00:07:26,351
Emma, do you watch sports on TV?

124
00:07:26,374 --> 00:07:31,322
No, I don’t watch much TV.

125
00:07:31,346 --> 00:07:35,646
What do you usually do on weekends?

126
00:07:35,669 --> 00:07:40,335
I play tennis with friends.

127
00:07:40,358 --> 00:07:43,325
Are you good at tennis?

128
00:07:43,348 --> 00:07:47,919
No, I’m still not very good.

129
00:07:47,943 --> 00:07:52,376
I can’t play tennis at all.

130
00:07:52,399 --> 00:07:58,474
Really? It’s a little difficult, but it’s fun!

131
00:07:58,497 --> 00:08:02,614
Could you teach me sometime?

132
00:08:02,638 --> 00:08:05,515
Sure, that’d be great!

133
00:08:05,538 --> 00:08:08,205
Let’s play together!

134
00:08:08,228 --> 00:08:09,728
Scene 4: Beverage Preferences

135
00:08:09,728 --> 00:08:11,795
Hello!

136
00:08:11,818 --> 00:08:14,612
Oh, hi there!

137
00:08:14,636 --> 00:08:18,936
What do you buy from the vending machine?

138
00:08:18,959 --> 00:08:22,392
I buy drinks.

139
00:08:22,415 --> 00:08:25,775
You must be thirsty.

140
00:08:25,798 --> 00:08:29,466
I’m really thirsty!

141
00:08:29,489 --> 00:08:33,323
It’s so hot today, isn’t it?

142
00:08:33,346 --> 00:08:39,212
On hot days, I usually drink cold water.

143
00:08:39,235 --> 00:08:41,821
Water?

144
00:08:41,845 --> 00:08:46,345
Emma, what do you drink?

145
00:08:46,368 --> 00:08:50,201
I always buy tea.

146
00:08:50,224 --> 00:08:53,409
Do you like tea?

147
00:08:53,433 --> 00:08:58,166
Yes, I love Japanese green tea!

148
00:08:58,189 --> 00:09:01,668
Really? Is it good?

149
00:09:01,692 --> 00:09:07,250
Yeah, cold green tea is really refreshing!

150
00:09:07,273 --> 00:09:10,430
Don’t you drink coffee?

151
00:09:10,454 --> 00:09:14,391
I don’t drink coffee much.

152
00:09:14,414 --> 00:09:18,848
I drink coffee often.

153
00:09:18,871 --> 00:09:21,815
Cold coffee?

154
00:09:21,838 --> 00:09:27,705
No, I always drink hot coffee.

155
00:09:27,728 --> 00:09:32,794
Wait, you drink hot coffee even in summer?

156
00:09:32,817 --> 00:09:37,951
Yes, because I like hot coffee.

157
00:09:37,974 --> 00:09:42,474
In summer, I always go for cold drinks.

158
00:09:42,497 --> 00:09:44,930
I see.

159
00:09:44,953 --> 00:09:50,734
You know, vending machine drinks are so convenient, aren't they?

160
00:09:50,758 --> 00:09:54,896
Yeah, but they're a bit expensive.

161
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:58,489
Supermarkets are cheaper, right?

162
00:09:58,512 --> 00:10:03,812
Oh, supermarkets are way cheaper.

163
00:10:03,835 --> 00:10:07,668
I usually buy mine at the supermarket.

164
00:10:07,691 --> 00:10:12,258
I don’t go to the supermarket much, though.

165
00:10:12,281 --> 00:10:14,755
Why not?

166
00:10:14,778 --> 00:10:19,133
It’s a little far from my place.

167
00:10:19,157 --> 00:10:21,590
It’s far?

168
00:10:21,613 --> 00:10:24,757
Do you have a bike?

169
00:10:24,781 --> 00:10:27,730
No, I don’t.

170
00:10:27,753 --> 00:10:32,429
Then walking there must be a hassle.

171
00:10:32,453 --> 00:10:38,286
Yeah, so I often use vending machines instead.

172
00:10:38,309 --> 00:10:41,612
Ah, I see.

173
00:10:41,636 --> 00:10:46,170
Oh, class is about to start soon.

174
00:10:46,193 --> 00:10:50,363
Yeah, let’s head back to the classroom.

175
00:10:50,387 --> 00:10:51,887
Scene 5: Grocery Shopping for Dinner

176
00:10:51,887 --> 00:10:54,762
Oh, Suzuki!

177
00:10:54,785 --> 00:10:58,361
Oh, Emma! Good evening.

178
00:10:58,384 --> 00:11:00,955
Good evening.

179
00:11:00,978 --> 00:11:03,412
Out shopping?

180
00:11:03,435 --> 00:11:05,584
Yep.

181
00:11:05,607 --> 00:11:08,678
Just picking up stuff for dinner.

182
00:11:08,702 --> 00:11:11,281
What a coincidence!

183
00:11:11,304 --> 00:11:15,372
I’m here for dinner groceries too.

184
00:11:15,396 --> 00:11:18,784
Do you always come to this supermarket?

185
00:11:18,808 --> 00:11:20,884
Yep.

186
00:11:20,907 --> 00:11:24,040
Yeah, it’s close to home.

187
00:11:24,063 --> 00:11:27,563
I come here often too.

188
00:11:27,586 --> 00:11:30,820
What are you buying today?

189
00:11:30,843 --> 00:11:34,029
Some veggies and meat.

190
00:11:34,052 --> 00:11:37,635
What are you making for dinner?

191
00:11:37,658 --> 00:11:40,296
I’m making curry.

192
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:42,953
That’s great!

193
00:11:42,976 --> 00:11:45,971
Do you like curry?

194
00:11:45,995 --> 00:11:48,028
Yep.

195
00:11:48,051 --> 00:11:50,718
I love it!

196
00:11:50,741 --> 00:11:53,774
Do you like it spicy?

197
00:11:53,797 --> 00:11:55,863
Yep.

198
00:11:55,886 --> 00:11:58,586
I love spicy food!

199
00:11:58,609 --> 00:12:04,276
I like curry too, but I can’t handle the spicy ones.

200
00:12:04,299 --> 00:12:06,532
I see.

201
00:12:06,555 --> 00:12:10,795
What are you making tonight, Emma?

202
00:12:10,818 --> 00:12:14,525
I’m grilling some fish.

203
00:12:14,549 --> 00:12:17,119
Fish, huh?

204
00:12:17,142 --> 00:12:19,618
Sounds delicious!

205
00:12:19,642 --> 00:12:21,777
Yep.

206
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:24,788
And I’ll make a salad too.

207
00:12:24,812 --> 00:12:27,681
You’re such a good cook!

208
00:12:27,704 --> 00:12:32,374
Oh no, not at all!

209
00:12:32,398 --> 00:12:35,739
I only know how to make curry.

210
00:12:35,763 --> 00:12:38,029
I see.

211
00:12:38,052 --> 00:12:41,786
You don’t make anything else?

212
00:12:41,809 --> 00:12:43,801
Nope.

213
00:12:43,824 --> 00:12:47,897
Other dishes are a bit tricky for me.

214
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:52,054
What do you *really* want to eat, though?

215
00:12:52,078 --> 00:12:56,811
I’d love to eat some delicious tempura!

216
00:12:56,834 --> 00:13:00,168
Tempura sounds great!

217
00:13:00,191 --> 00:13:05,024
But it's so hard to make at home.

218
00:13:05,047 --> 00:13:07,115
Nope.

219
00:13:07,138 --> 00:13:10,572
Tempura is really tricky.

220
00:13:10,595 --> 00:13:15,583
That's why I usually eat it at restaurants.

221
00:13:15,606 --> 00:13:18,673
The one near the station?

222
00:13:18,696 --> 00:13:20,929
Yep.

223
00:13:20,952 --> 00:13:25,019
Their tempura is delicious, you know.

224
00:13:25,042 --> 00:13:27,675
Oh, really?

225
00:13:27,698 --> 00:13:31,447
I'll have to try it sometime.

226
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:36,241
Well, I'm off to the meat section.

227
00:13:36,265 --> 00:13:38,044
Yep.

228
00:13:38,068 --> 00:13:40,426
See you tomorrow.

229
00:13:40,449 --> 00:13:42,751
See you tomorrow.

230
00:13:42,775 --> 00:13:44,275
Scene 6: Conversation on the Way Home

231
00:13:44,275 --> 00:13:47,027
Goodbye.

232
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:50,621
Oh, Emma!

233
00:13:50,645 --> 00:13:53,383
Want to walk home together?

234
00:13:53,407 --> 00:13:56,907
Sure, let's go.

235
00:13:56,930 --> 00:14:01,911
How do you get home, Emma?

236
00:14:01,935 --> 00:14:05,568
I take the train.

237
00:14:05,591 --> 00:14:08,098
The train, huh?

238
00:14:08,122 --> 00:14:11,655
Which station do you get off at?

239
00:14:11,678 --> 00:14:15,116
Shinjuku Station.

240
00:14:15,139 --> 00:14:17,730
Shinjuku?

241
00:14:17,754 --> 00:14:21,588
It's great for shopping, isn't it?

242
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:25,481
Yeah, it's super convenient.

243
00:14:25,504 --> 00:14:31,604
How long does it take from school to Shinjuku?

244
00:14:31,627 --> 00:14:35,460
About 20 minutes by train.

245
00:14:35,483 --> 00:14:38,517
That's pretty close.

246
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:42,659
How about you, Suzuki?

247
00:14:42,682 --> 00:14:46,149
I take the bus.

248
00:14:46,172 --> 00:14:48,720
The bus?

249
00:14:48,744 --> 00:14:52,712
How long does that take?

250
00:14:52,735 --> 00:14:56,238
Around 40 minutes.

251
00:14:56,262 --> 00:14:59,895
That's a bit far.

252
00:14:59,918 --> 00:15:04,951
Yeah, but at least I can sit the whole way.

253
00:15:04,974 --> 00:15:07,874
That's great!

254
00:15:07,897 --> 00:15:12,576
The train is always so crowded.

255
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:15,373
Is it crowded in the morning too?

256
00:15:15,396 --> 00:15:20,029
Yeah, it's really packed.

257
00:15:20,052 --> 00:15:22,952
That sounds tough.

258
00:15:22,976 --> 00:15:27,209
It is, but I'm used to it now.

259
00:15:27,232 --> 00:15:30,821
Do you walk from the station to your place?

260
00:15:30,845 --> 00:15:35,678
Yeah, it's about a 10-minute walk.

261
00:15:35,701 --> 00:15:38,257
That's close.

262
00:15:38,281 --> 00:15:42,514
I'm just 5 minutes from the bus stop.

263
00:15:42,537 --> 00:15:45,571
That's convenient.

264
00:15:45,594 --> 00:15:50,533
Yeah, though rainy days are a bit rough.

265
00:15:50,556 --> 00:15:53,623
Tell me about it.

266
00:15:53,646 --> 00:15:57,379
Good thing the weather's nice today.

267
00:15:57,402 --> 00:16:02,469
Yeah, oh—we're at the station already.

268
00:16:02,492 --> 00:16:06,392
I'll catch my train from here.

269
00:16:06,415 --> 00:16:11,891
Ah, my bus stop is over there too.

270
00:16:11,914 --> 00:16:15,647
Well, I'll see you here today then.

271
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:19,259
See you tomorrow!

272
00:16:19,282 --> 00:16:21,669
Take care.

273
00:16:21,693 --> 00:16:23,193
Scene 7: Weekend Plans

274
00:16:23,193 --> 00:16:27,307
You must be tired after this week. Great job!

275
00:16:27,331 --> 00:16:30,041
Good work today!

276
00:16:30,064 --> 00:16:32,797
Are you heading home now?

277
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:36,599
Yes, I'm about to leave.

278
00:16:36,622 --> 00:16:40,656
You worked out a lot today, huh?

279
00:16:40,679 --> 00:16:44,718
Yeah, I'm a little tired.

280
00:16:44,742 --> 00:16:47,814
Do you have work tomorrow?

281
00:16:47,837 --> 00:16:52,006
No, I have the day off.

282
00:16:52,030 --> 00:16:57,200
I see. What are your plans for the weekend?

283
00:16:57,224 --> 00:17:01,124
I'm going to see a movie with friends.

284
00:17:01,147 --> 00:17:05,280
A movie? That sounds nice.

285
00:17:05,304 --> 00:17:10,179
Yeah, it's a new one.

286
00:17:10,203 --> 00:17:12,595
What kind of movie is it?

287
00:17:12,618 --> 00:17:15,552
An action movie.

288
00:17:15,575 --> 00:17:18,442
That sounds exciting!

289
00:17:18,465 --> 00:17:22,904
What about you, Emma? What are you doing this weekend?

290
00:17:22,927 --> 00:17:26,761
I'm going to the mountains.

291
00:17:26,783 --> 00:17:31,136
The mountains? Are you going alone?

292
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:35,293
No, I'm going with my family.

293
00:17:35,316 --> 00:17:38,216
That's great!

294
00:17:38,239 --> 00:17:42,672
I'll take lots of photos in the mountains.

295
00:17:42,695 --> 00:17:45,433
Do you like taking photos?

296
00:17:45,457 --> 00:17:49,091
Yes, I love it.

297
00:17:49,115 --> 00:17:52,622
What kind of photos do you take?

298
00:17:52,645 --> 00:17:56,199
I take pictures of scenery and flowers.

299
00:17:56,223 --> 00:18:00,756
They must be beautiful. I'd love to see them.

300
00:18:00,779 --> 00:18:05,646
Well, I'll show you the photos at the gym next week.

301
00:18:05,669 --> 00:18:08,369
Sure, I'd like that.

302
00:18:08,392 --> 00:18:12,726
Hope the weather is nice on Sunday.

303
00:18:12,749 --> 00:18:17,449
Yeah, I think it'll be sunny.

304
00:18:17,472 --> 00:18:20,011
Thank you!

305
00:18:20,034 --> 00:18:22,313
Yep.

306
00:18:22,337 --> 00:18:26,839
Enjoy your movie tomorrow!

307
00:18:26,862 --> 00:18:30,595
What are you doing after the movie?

308
00:18:30,618 --> 00:18:34,695
I'm going to grab a meal with friends.

309
00:18:34,719 --> 00:18:38,352
Sounds like you'll have a fun weekend.

310
00:18:38,375 --> 00:18:42,923
Yeah. See you next week!

311
00:18:42,947 --> 00:18:46,414
See you next week!

312
00:18:46,437 --> 00:18:47,937
Scene 8: How to Memorize Kanji

313
00:18:47,937 --> 00:18:49,929
Hello!

314
00:18:49,952 --> 00:18:52,728
Oh, hi there!

315
00:18:52,752 --> 00:18:56,885
Have you been studying in the library this whole time?

316
00:18:56,908 --> 00:19:01,208
Yeah, I studied for about an hour.

317
00:19:01,231 --> 00:19:05,669
I see. Good work!

318
00:19:05,692 --> 00:19:09,485
Studying Japanese is tough, isn't it?

319
00:19:09,508 --> 00:19:13,175
What do you find the hardest?

320
00:19:13,198 --> 00:19:18,237
Kanji is the hardest for me.

321
00:19:18,261 --> 00:19:22,648
There are so many kanji, after all.

322
00:19:22,671 --> 00:19:27,171
Memorizing them is really challenging.

323
00:19:27,194 --> 00:19:31,363
How do you memorize kanji?

324
00:19:31,387 --> 00:19:36,820
I write them repeatedly in my notebook.

325
00:19:36,843 --> 00:19:39,910
You memorize them by writing, huh?

326
00:19:39,933 --> 00:19:42,366
That’s great!

327
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:46,822
What about you, Emma? What do you find difficult?

328
00:19:46,845 --> 00:19:51,824
Listening is really tough for me.

329
00:19:51,848 --> 00:19:54,606
You mean listening?

330
00:19:54,629 --> 00:20:00,529
Yeah, because Japanese people speak so fast.

331
00:20:00,552 --> 00:20:05,666
True. I sometimes don’t catch it either.

332
00:20:05,690 --> 00:20:09,863
Do you watch anime or dramas?

333
00:20:09,886 --> 00:20:13,804
Yeah, I watch them a lot.

334
00:20:13,828 --> 00:20:18,895
Japanese dramas are great for practicing listening.

335
00:20:18,918 --> 00:20:24,553
Really? Then I’ll watch more from now on.

336
00:20:24,576 --> 00:20:29,761
What do you enjoy most about learning Japanese?

337
00:20:29,785 --> 00:20:34,618
I love having conversations the most.

338
00:20:34,641 --> 00:20:37,751
You mean speaking?

339
00:20:37,775 --> 00:20:43,642
Yes! Talking with friends in Japanese is so much fun.

340
00:20:43,665 --> 00:20:47,768
I love conversations too.

341
00:20:47,791 --> 00:20:51,379
Do you often chat with classmates?

342
00:20:51,402 --> 00:20:56,151
Yeah, we talk a lot during breaks.

343
00:20:56,174 --> 00:20:59,250
That's great!

344
00:20:59,274 --> 00:21:02,907
Do you study on weekends too?

345
00:21:02,930 --> 00:21:07,297
Yes, I study a little.

346
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:10,620
Keep up the good work!

347
00:21:10,643 --> 00:21:13,343
Thank you!

348
00:21:13,366 --> 00:21:14,866
Scene 9: Daily Conversation – Weekend Activities

349
00:21:14,866 --> 00:21:17,999
Oh, Suzuki!

350
00:21:18,022 --> 00:21:20,926
Oh, Emma!

351
00:21:20,950 --> 00:21:23,584
Good morning!

352
00:21:23,607 --> 00:21:26,440
Good morning!

353
00:21:26,463 --> 00:21:29,563
Heading to school now?

354
00:21:29,586 --> 00:21:33,019
Yes, that's right.

355
00:21:33,042 --> 00:21:36,776
Yesterday was Sunday, right?

356
00:21:36,799 --> 00:21:39,708
What did you do?

357
00:21:39,731 --> 00:21:44,198
I went to Yokohama yesterday.

358
00:21:44,222 --> 00:21:47,218
Yokohama?

359
00:21:47,241 --> 00:21:49,508
That’s great!

360
00:21:49,531 --> 00:21:53,631
Yeah, it was so much fun!

361
00:21:53,654 --> 00:21:56,793
Who did you go with?

362
00:21:56,817 --> 00:22:00,524
I went with friends.

363
00:22:00,547 --> 00:22:04,981
What did you do in Yokohama?

364
00:22:05,004 --> 00:22:07,684
We saw the ocean.

365
00:22:07,707 --> 00:22:10,374
It was really beautiful.

366
00:22:10,397 --> 00:22:14,137
What did you do after that?

367
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:18,130
We ate at Chinatown.

368
00:22:18,153 --> 00:22:21,187
Chinatown?

369
00:22:21,210 --> 00:22:24,396
What did you eat?

370
00:22:24,420 --> 00:22:28,402
Ramen and dumplings.

371
00:22:28,425 --> 00:22:31,459
Was it good?

372
00:22:31,482 --> 00:22:35,859
Yes, it was delicious!

373
00:22:35,882 --> 00:22:38,415
That’s great!

374
00:22:38,439 --> 00:22:42,550
I want to go to Chinatown too.

375
00:22:42,573 --> 00:22:47,007
What did you do yesterday, Emma?

376
00:22:47,030 --> 00:22:52,463
I stayed home all day.

377
00:22:52,486 --> 00:22:55,553
What did you do at home?

378
00:22:55,576 --> 00:22:59,972
I cleaned my room in the morning.

379
00:22:59,995 --> 00:23:02,828
I see.

380
00:23:02,851 --> 00:23:05,395
That sounds tough.

381
00:23:05,419 --> 00:23:09,486
Yeah, I'm a little tired.

382
00:23:09,509 --> 00:23:12,876
What did you do after that?

383
00:23:12,899 --> 00:23:16,732
I read a book in the afternoon.

384
00:23:16,755 --> 00:23:19,622
What kind of book?

385
00:23:19,645 --> 00:23:23,178
A Japanese novel.

386
00:23:23,201 --> 00:23:26,701
A novel in Japanese?

387
00:23:26,724 --> 00:23:29,424
That’s amazing!

388
00:23:29,447 --> 00:23:34,184
No, it's still a bit difficult for me.

389
00:23:34,207 --> 00:23:37,207
Do you use a dictionary?

390
00:23:37,231 --> 00:23:43,134
Yes, I read slowly while using a dictionary.

391
00:23:43,157 --> 00:23:46,632
This is really educational.

392
00:23:46,655 --> 00:23:48,759
Yep.

393
00:23:48,783 --> 00:23:52,417
Oh, the train is here.

394
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:55,273
Let's get on.

395
00:23:55,296 --> 00:23:56,796
Scene 10: Autumn Conversations

396
00:23:56,796 --> 00:23:58,833
Hello!

397
00:23:58,856 --> 00:24:01,763
Oh, hi there!

398
00:24:01,787 --> 00:24:05,892
Do you often drink coffee here?

399
00:24:05,916 --> 00:24:09,549
Yes, I come here sometimes.

400
00:24:09,572 --> 00:24:13,916
This is my first time here today.

401
00:24:13,939 --> 00:24:17,808
Their coffee here is really good.

402
00:24:17,832 --> 00:24:21,665
Is that so? I'm looking forward to it.

403
00:24:21,688 --> 00:24:25,924
It's gotten quite cold lately, hasn't it?

404
00:24:25,948 --> 00:24:30,115
Yes, it's really cold.

405
00:24:30,138 --> 00:24:33,873
It's already November, after all.

406
00:24:33,897 --> 00:24:36,242
It's autumn.

407
00:24:36,265 --> 00:24:40,001
Yes, it's the autumn season.

408
00:24:40,024 --> 00:24:44,558
Autumn is my favorite season.

409
00:24:44,581 --> 00:24:46,539
Why is that?

410
00:24:46,562 --> 00:24:50,540
Because the food is so delicious.

411
00:24:50,563 --> 00:24:55,497
That's true. Autumn fruits are especially good.

412
00:24:55,520 --> 00:24:59,953
Suzuki, which season do you like best?

413
00:24:59,976 --> 00:25:03,493
I like spring.

414
00:25:03,517 --> 00:25:06,650
Cherry blossom season, right?

415
00:25:06,673 --> 00:25:10,973
Yes, because the cherry blossoms are so beautiful.

416
00:25:10,996 --> 00:25:15,935
But spring can be quite windy, don't you think?

417
00:25:15,959 --> 00:25:18,308
Yeah, it is.

418
00:25:18,331 --> 00:25:23,064
It's gotten colder, how are you feeling?

419
00:25:23,087 --> 00:25:27,587
Actually, I caught a bit of a cold.

420
00:25:27,610 --> 00:25:30,043
Are you okay?

421
00:25:30,066 --> 00:25:34,933
Yes, I took some medicine, so I'm fine now.

422
00:25:34,956 --> 00:25:40,389
Make sure to go home early today and get some rest under warm covers.

423
00:25:40,412 --> 00:25:42,729
Thank you!

424
00:25:42,753 --> 00:25:46,023
How about you, Emma? Are you okay?

425
00:25:46,046 --> 00:25:49,546
I'm fine.

426
00:25:49,569 --> 00:25:52,278
That's good to hear.

427
00:25:52,302 --> 00:25:56,294
I exercise every morning, so I stay healthy.

428
00:25:56,317 --> 00:25:58,817
What kind of exercise do you do?

429
00:25:58,840 --> 00:26:02,607
I walk in the nearby park.

430
00:26:02,630 --> 00:26:05,864
That's great for your health.

431
00:26:05,887 --> 00:26:10,387
Yes, that's why I never catch colds.

432
00:26:10,410 --> 00:26:14,276
I think I'll start walking a bit from tomorrow too.

433
00:26:14,299 --> 00:26:18,233
Then, shall we walk together?

434
00:26:18,256 --> 00:26:21,389
Sure, I'd like that.